{
  "info": {
    "name": "Wallet Transfer Service",
    "description": "Postman collection aligned with the Wallet Transfer Service APIs, response codes, and integration test scenarios.\n\n**Base URL:** `{{baseUrl}}`\n**Swagger UI:** `http://localhost:8080/api/wallet-transfer/swagger-ui.html`\n\n**Seeded wallets (local profile via data.sql):**\n| Wallet | Initial balance |\n|--------|------------------|\n| wallet_1 | 100000 |\n| wallet_2 | 50000 |\n| wallet_3 | 0 |\n\n**Response envelope:** `{ status, message, responseCode, data }`\n\n**Success codes:**\n- 20001 — Transfer processed\n- 20002 — Balance fetched\n- 20003 — History fetched\n\n**Error codes:**\n- 5001 — Transfer failed (generic business failure)\n- 5002 — Insufficient funds\n- 5003 — Idempotency key conflict\n- 5113 — Wallet not found\n- 6017 — Validation / invalid request\n- 5000 — Unexpected server error\n\n**Notes:**\n- Run transfer scenarios with unique `idempotencyKey` values when re-testing on a non-fresh database.\n- Requests include Postman test scripts asserting `responseCode` and key behavior.\n- For true concurrency testing, use the integration test suite (`TransferIntegrationTest`).",
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080/api/wallet-transfer"
    },
    {
      "key": "e2eIdempotencyKey",
      "value": "postman-e2e-placeholder"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Transfers",
      "description": "POST /v1/transfers — idempotent wallet-to-wallet transfers with double-entry ledger.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 - Successful Transfer",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('responseCode 20001', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().responseCode).to.eql(20001));",
                  "pm.test('status SUCCESS', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('SUCCESS'));",
                  "pm.test('transfer PROCESSED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.status).to.eql('PROCESSED'));",
                  "pm.test('two ledger entries', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.ledgerEntries).to.have.lengthOf(2));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"postman-success-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"fromWalletId\": \"wallet_1\",\n  \"toWalletId\": \"wallet_2\",\n  \"amount\": 100\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/transfers",
            "description": "Happy path. Expect responseCode 20001, data.status PROCESSED, DEBIT + CREDIT ledger entries."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "02 - Idempotent Replay (Same Key + Payload)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('replayIdempotencyKey')) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('replayIdempotencyKey', 'postman-replay-' + Date.now());",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('replayFirstResponse')) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('replayFirstResponse', pm.response.text());",
                  "  pm.test('first call PROCESSED', () => pm.expect(body.data.status).to.eql('PROCESSED'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('identical response on replay', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('replayFirstResponse')));",
                  "  pm.test('responseCode 20001 on replay', () => pm.expect(body.responseCode).to.eql(20001));",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"{{replayIdempotencyKey}}\",\n  \"fromWalletId\": \"wallet_1\",\n  \"toWalletId\": \"wallet_2\",\n  \"amount\": 50\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/transfers",
            "description": "Run this request twice in a row (same collection variable key). Second call must return an identical body without double-debiting."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "03 - Insufficient Funds",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('responseCode 5002', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().responseCode).to.eql(5002));",
                  "pm.test('status FAIL', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('FAIL'));",
                  "pm.test('transfer FAILED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.status).to.eql('FAILED'));",
                  "pm.test('no ledger entries', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.ledgerEntries).to.be.empty);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"postman-insufficient-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"fromWalletId\": \"wallet_3\",\n  \"toWalletId\": \"wallet_2\",\n  \"amount\": 10\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/transfers",
            "description": "wallet_3 has zero balance. Expect responseCode 5002, data.status FAILED, empty ledgerEntries."
          }
        },
